/target
/docs/book

# Playwright MCP session artifacts: page snapshots, console logs, screenshots.
.playwright-mcp/

# cargo-mutants output (caught/missed/unviable/timeout lists, per-mutant logs, and
# a full scratch copy of the tree). CI uploads it as an artifact; locally it is
# regenerable. Under jj this is not merely tidiness — the working copy is
# snapshotted on every command, so an unignored mutants.out lands in whatever
# commit happens to be @ without anyone running an add.
/mutants.out/
/mutants.out.old/

# Fuzzing. The canonical corpus lives in the nightly's GitHub Actions cache, not in
# git — it grows without bound and is regenerable, so committing it would add
# megabytes per night for nothing. What IS committed is the hand-written `seed-*`
# inputs, which are the starting points a fresh clone (or a cold cache) fuzzes from.
/fuzz/target/
/fuzz/artifacts/
/fuzz/coverage/
/fuzz/corpus/*/*
!/fuzz/corpus/*/seed-*
